[3] Unital-style tangent/secant lesson
  MathWorld's geometric-combinatorics unital is a 2-(q^3+1,q+1,1) design.
  LRC transfer: choose a tangent sector/anchor, then demand controlled pair incidence
  before scalarizing.  Clebsch closed neighborhoods give a nearby exact 2-(16,6,2)
  design; this is the finite covariance object, while scalar additive energy forgets
  tangent/secant labels.

